{"authored" [{"question" "q-334265" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution of the Clairaut differential equation:\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}-7{y}^{′}.\n$$" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-334265/review.json" "file_sha256" "f621aa21f0a1015197aaa7088c7990d43475f2ede2dce2f2398241de3169db56" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-334265/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "eae685b15e798d3b0bc799c94ce25bed2f05c68c3127a685fbc8224b1ddfa63d" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-334265/verification.json" "basis" 1808 "rationale" "The source substitutes p=c into y=xp-7p′ even though its undifferentiated equation is y=xp-7p. Remove the erroneous prime in this one substitution statement. General answer y=cx-7c, problem, choices, fields and answers are unchanged."} {"question" "q-334265" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}-7{y}^{′},\n$$\n\nwe start by setting\n$p={y}^{′}.$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=xp-7p.\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={(xp-7p)}^{′} \\\\ p & =p+x{p}^{′}-7{p}^{′} \\\\ 0 & ={p}^{′}(x-7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product on the right-hand side equals zero, which means at least one of the factors must be zero.\n\nThe general solution of the Clairaut differential equation is obtained if ${p}^{′}=0.$ Then, $p$ is constant, say \n\n$$\np=c.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $p=c$ into $y=xp-7p,$ we get the general solution\n\n$$\ny=cx-7c.\n$$\n\nThis represents a family of straight lines, one line for each constant value of $c.$" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-334265/review.json" "file_sha256" "f621aa21f0a1015197aaa7088c7990d43475f2ede2dce2f2398241de3169db56" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-334265/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "eae685b15e798d3b0bc799c94ce25bed2f05c68c3127a685fbc8224b1ddfa63d" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-334265/verification.json" "basis" 1808 "rationale" "The source substitutes p=c into y=xp-7p′ even though its undifferentiated equation is y=xp-7p. Remove the erroneous prime in this one substitution statement. General answer y=cx-7c, problem, choices, fields and answers are unchanged."} {"question" "q-334265" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=cx-7c"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-334265/review.json" "file_sha256" "f621aa21f0a1015197aaa7088c7990d43475f2ede2dce2f2398241de3169db56" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-334265/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "eae685b15e798d3b0bc799c94ce25bed2f05c68c3127a685fbc8224b1ddfa63d" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-334265/verification.json" "basis" 1808 "rationale" "The source substitutes p=c into y=xp-7p′ even though its undifferentiated equation is y=xp-7p. Remove the erroneous prime in this one substitution statement. General answer y=cx-7c, problem, choices, fields and answers are unchanged."} {"question" "q-334265" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution of the Clairaut differential equation:\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}-7{y}^{′}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054585/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b6f52bf096bc